---
import SectionHeading from "./CaseSectionHeading.astro";
import MediaFrame from "./ProductMediaFrame.astro";
import AnimatedGif from "./AnimatedGif.astro";
import selectorPlacement from "../assets/caddy/graphics/caddy-placement-banner.png";
import v1DemoGif from "../assets/gifs/caddy/caddy-v1-demo.gif?url";
import v1DemoStill from "../assets/gifs/caddy/caddy-v1-demo-still.png";
---

<div class="caddy-quick">
  <section id="overview">
    <SectionHeading number="01" eyebrow="Overview" title="The shopping experience around an AI recommendation assistant." />
    <p class="ownership">I designed how customers enter the conversation, understand the recommendation, and move toward a product.</p>
    <p class="section-intro">I owned the UI direction, UX recommendations, early concepts, Figma design, starter prompts, category entry points, recommendation presentation, product-card experience, and ongoing design iteration.</p>
    <p class="boundary"><strong>Ownership boundary:</strong> I did not build the underlying AI model, train it, or own the backend recommendation logic.</p>
    <div class="overview-context">
      <div><span>Status</span><strong>Live and actively evolving</strong></div>
      <div><span>Product</span><strong>Consumer shopping experience</strong></div>
      <div><span>Focus</span><strong>Make recommendations easier to act on</strong></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="problem">
    <SectionHeading number="02" eyebrow="The problem" title="A useful answer was not automatically a useful shopping experience." />
    <p class="section-intro">Traditional selectors relied on fixed questions and a limited recommendation set. Conversation created room for more context and follow-up, but the early recommendation experience was still text-heavy and difficult to evaluate at a glance.</p>
    <div class="discovery-shift" role="img" aria-label="Product discovery evolved from a fixed selector to a conversation, then from a text-heavy recommendation to a more familiar shopping experience.">
      <div><span>Traditional selector</span><strong>Fixed questions</strong></div>
      <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
      <div><span>Conversational AI</span><strong>More context and follow-up</strong></div>
      <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
      <div class="accent"><span>Product experience</span><strong>Recommendations people can shop</strong></div>
    </div>
    <div class="problem-proof">
      <div>
        <p class="story-label">Discovery context</p>
        <h3>Caddy entered an ecosystem of familiar guided selector tools.</h3>
        <p>The opportunity was not simply to replace a form with a chat box. The conversation still needed to help customers understand what to consider and what to do next.</p>
      </div>
      <MediaFrame label="Caddy and traditional selector tools">
        <img src={selectorPlacement.src} width={selectorPlacement.width} height={selectorPlacement.height} alt="Callaway selector-tools page presenting Caddy above traditional driver, fairway wood, iron, wedge, putter, and golf-ball selectors." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </MediaFrame>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="built">
    <SectionHeading number="03" eyebrow="What I changed" title="I moved the recommendation toward familiar ecommerce patterns." />
    <div class="change-intro">
      <div>
        <p class="story-label">Early recommendation experience</p>
        <h3>The answer carried useful product information, but customers still had to work to shop it.</h3>
      </div>
      <p>My design direction brought product imagery, pricing, clearer hierarchy, and recognizable shopping actions into the recommendation experience.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="v1-media">
      <MediaFrame label="Early conversation and recommendation flow" motion>
        <AnimatedGif src={v1DemoGif} fallbackSrc={v1DemoStill.src} width={v1DemoStill.width} height={v1DemoStill.height} alt="Early Caddy mobile flow showing a customer question, conversational follow-up, product recommendations, and an email-summary handoff." />
      </MediaFrame>
      <div class="commerce-patterns" aria-label="Shopping experience improvements">
        <div><span>01</span><strong>Product imagery</strong><p>Make recommendations recognizable.</p></div>
        <div><span>02</span><strong>Price and hierarchy</strong><p>Make options easier to compare.</p></div>
        <div><span>03</span><strong>Shopping actions</strong><p>Connect advice to a next step.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="live-note"><strong>Visible in the current live experience:</strong> guided example questions, conversational recommendations, and a separate product panel with imagery, pricing, and shopping links.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="impact">
    <SectionHeading number="04" eyebrow="Impact" title="The experience is live—and the recommendations are connected to shopping actions." />
    <div class="impact-grid">
      <div><span>Status</span><strong>Live</strong><p>Dedicated experience on CallawayGolf.com</p></div>
      <div><span>Entry</span><strong>Guided</strong><p>Categories and example questions help people begin</p></div>
      <div><span>Recommendation</span><strong>Visual</strong><p>Product imagery and pricing support evaluation</p></div>
      <div><span>Next step</span><strong>Shop</strong><p>Recommended products connect to shopping links</p></div>
    </div>
    <a class="live-link" href="https://www.callawaygolf.com/the-caddy?source=cg-home-page" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View the live Caddy experience <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </section>

  <section id="why">
    <SectionHeading number="05" eyebrow="Why it worked" title="The interface treated the recommendation as the beginning of a shopping decision—not the end of a conversation." />
    <blockquote>“The model was not the product. The experience around its answer was.”</blockquote>
    <p class="section-intro">The design used patterns customers already understood: guided entry, visible products, clear hierarchy, pricing, and direct shopping actions. AI supplied the recommendation; product design made it understandable and usable.</p>
    <div class="responsibility-model">
      <div><span>My focus</span><strong>Entry, interaction, presentation, and ongoing UX iteration</strong></div>
      <div><span>Partner system</span><strong>AI model, training, and backend recommendation logic</strong></div>
    </div>
    <div class="deep-dive-cta">
      <div><p class="story-label">Want the design evolution?</p><h3>Explore the selector comparison, early concepts, recommendation limitations, ownership boundaries, and future product explorations.</h3></div>
      <button class="button-link" type="button" data-deep-toggle aria-controls="deep-dive" aria-expanded="false"><span data-deep-toggle-label>Read the Deep Dive</span> <span data-deep-toggle-icon aria-hidden="true">↓</span></button>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<style>
  .caddy-quick > section { padding-block: var(--space-8); border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--header-height) + var(--space-7)); }
  .ownership { margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); font-size: var(--step-2); font-weight: 680; line-height: 1.25; }
  .section-intro { margin: 0 0 var(--space-5); color: var(--color-text-soft); font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .boundary, .live-note { margin: 0; padding: var(--space-4); border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) 4%, var(--color-surface)); color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  .story-label, .overview-context span, .discovery-shift span, .commerce-patterns span, .impact-grid span, .responsibility-model span { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.07em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .overview-context { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); margin-top: var(--space-6); border-block: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .overview-context div { display: grid; gap: var(--space-2); padding: var(--space-4); border-right: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .overview-context div:first-child { padding-left: 0; }
  .overview-context div:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .overview-context strong { font-size: var(--step--1); }
  .discovery-shift { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr; align-items: stretch; margin-bottom: var(--space-7); }
  .discovery-shift > div { display: flex; min-height: 8.5rem; flex-direction: column; padding: var(--space-4); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .discovery-shift > div.accent { border-color: var(--color-accent); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) 5%, transparent); }
  .discovery-shift strong { margin-top: auto; font-size: var(--step--1); }
  .discovery-shift i { align-self: center; padding: var(--space-2); color: var(--color-accent); font-style: normal; }
  .problem-proof { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.42fr) minmax(18rem, 0.58fr); gap: var(--space-6); align-items: center; }
  .problem-proof h3, .problem-proof p { margin-top: 0; }
  .problem-proof p:last-child { color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  .problem-proof :global(.media-window) { height: 35rem; }
  .problem-proof :global(img) { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: contain; }
  .change-intro { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 0.52fr 0.48fr; gap: var(--space-6); margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .change-intro h3, .change-intro p { margin: 0; }
  .change-intro > p { color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  .v1-media { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-5); align-items: stretch; }
  .v1-media :global(.media-window) { aspect-ratio: 16 / 10; }
  .v1-media :global(.gif-player img) { object-fit: contain; }
  .commerce-patterns { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); border-block: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong); }
  .commerce-patterns > div { display: flex; min-height: 9rem; flex-direction: column; padding: var(--space-4); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .commerce-patterns > div { border-right: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .commerce-patterns > div:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .commerce-patterns strong { margin-top: auto; font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .commerce-patterns p { margin: var(--space-2) 0 0; color: var(--color-text-soft); font-size: var(--step--1); }
  .live-note { margin-top: var(--space-5); }
  .impact-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); border-block: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong); }
  .impact-grid > div { display: flex; min-height: 10rem; flex-direction: column; padding: var(--space-5); border-right: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .impact-grid > div:nth-child(2n) { border-right: 0; }
  .impact-grid strong { margin-top: auto; color: var(--color-accent); font-size: var(--step-3); line-height: 1; }
  .impact-grid p { margin: var(--space-2) 0 0; color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  .live-link { display: inline-flex; min-height: 2.75rem; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-2); margin-top: var(--space-4); color: var(--color-accent); font-weight: 700; }
  blockquote { margin: 0 0 var(--space-5); padding-left: var(--space-4); border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent); font-size: var(--step-2); font-weight: 680; line-height: 1.25; }
  .responsibility-model { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); border-block: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .responsibility-model > div { display: flex; min-height: 8rem; flex-direction: column; padding: var(--space-4); border-right: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .responsibility-model > div:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .responsibility-model strong { margin-top: auto; padding-top: var(--space-4); }
  .deep-dive-cta { display: flex; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--space-6); margin-top: var(--space-7); padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong); background: var(--color-surface); }
  .deep-dive-cta h3 { max-width: 36rem; margin: 0; }
  .deep-dive-cta .button-link { flex: 0 0 auto; }
  @media (max-width: 46rem) {
    .overview-context, .problem-proof, .change-intro, .responsibility-model { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .overview-context div { padding-inline: 0; border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
    .overview-context div:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
    .discovery-shift { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .discovery-shift > div { min-height: 6rem; }
    .discovery-shift i { transform: rotate(90deg); }
    .commerce-patterns { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .commerce-patterns > div { border-right: 0; }
    .responsibility-model > div { border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
    .responsibility-model > div:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
    .deep-dive-cta { align-items: stretch; flex-direction: column; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    .impact-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .impact-grid > div { border-right: 0; }
    .v1-media :global(.media-window) { aspect-ratio: 4 / 5; }
  }
</style>
